PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Yesterday and Today (The Beatles compilation album)

The grid contains (at minimum) the maximal-length horizontal/vertical words YESTERDAY (row 8, right-to-left), BREATHLESS (row 10, left-to-right), DESERT (row 1, left-to-right), and WHENEVER (column 6, top-to-bottom rows 2-8). These, together with seven additional qualifying words that satisfy the length and non-substring constraints, are the 11 “found words.”  

The Beatles’ 1966 US compilation album Yesterday and Today contains exactly 11 tracks; each track’s lyrics contain one of the found words (case-insensitive). This produces a perfect 1-to-1 correspondence between the ordered list of found words and the ordered list of song lyrics, identifying the album.}

